# Testing Documentation Sync

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

When test behavior, test scope, or test execution workflow changes, update
the testing docs in the same task:

| Page | Holds |
|------|-------|
| `HPCPerfStats/docs/how-to/develop/run-tests.md` | Prerequisites, commands, compose workflows, opt-in suites, frontend build and tests, coverage, accessibility, git hooks and static analysis, memory profiling, troubleshooting |
| `HPCPerfStats/docs/reference/test-layout.md` | Test layers, where tests live, markers and gates, runners, test modules, contract tests, frontend coverage, pre-merge matrix |
| `HPCPerfStats/docs/how-to/develop/run-sync-timedb-benchmarks.md` | sync_timedb benchmark and loaded-soak procedure (earlier results: `docs/history/sync-timedb-throughput-campaign.md`) |
| `HPCPerfStats/docs/how-to/develop/diagnose-update-metrics.md` | update_metrics diagnosis workflow, columnar parity, stall reasons |

## Trigger conditions
- New/removed/renamed test files.
- Changes to test commands, markers, fixtures, or test dependencies.
- Changes to **committed** Bokeh `json_item` fixtures under `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/test/fixtures/` or to how they are generated (regeneration commands, Django entrypoints, Playwright CDN pin). Keep `docs/how-to/develop/run-tests.md` aligned with `web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc` → **Bokeh job-list `json_item` fixtures**.
- Changes to test runners/scripts (for example `scripts/run_tests.py`,
  `tests/run_web_e2e_workflow.sh`, compose-based test workflows, or
  `pyproject.toml` test runner metadata).
- Changes to test prerequisites (DB/Valkey/Playwright/setup steps).

## Required actions
- Update the page from the table above that holds the changed commands, scope, or prerequisites.
- **Run logs and local runtime artifacts** belong under **`test_runs/`** per **`test-runs-output-directory.mdc`** — do not add new **`docs/test_run_log_*.md`** files.
- When **`testing-best-practices.mdc`** changes, sync `docs/reference/test-layout.md` (Test layers, Where tests live, Pre-merge matrix) in the same task.
- Keep examples copy-paste ready and consistent with current scripts/config.
- Include both quick-start commands and any specialized runners when applicable.
- Describe the current test setup only, per `docs-current-state-only.mdc`: no document history table, no notes on removed tests or old flags, no "previously"/"now" phrasing.

## Verification
- Confirm documented commands/paths match current repository files.
- For non-doc-only testing changes, run the relevant tests after updates.
